    {
      "id": 8,
      "title": "Active alert policies (from infra/envs/stg/monitoring.tf)",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 24
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "| Policy | Condition | Threshold |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cloud_run_errors` | Cloud Run service/job emits an ERROR-severity log | any |\n| `outbox_relay_dead_letter` | outbox relay job logs `dead_letter > 0` | any |\n| `pubsub_dlq_backlog` | `num_undelivered_messages` on `goatos-stg-outbox-events-dlq-inspect` | > 0 for 5m |\n| `cloud_sql_cpu` | Cloud SQL CPU utilization | > 80% for 5m |\n| `api_error_rate_slo_burn` | 5xx rate / total rate | > 1% for 5m (SLO 99.5%) |\n| `api_latency_p99_burn` | read-path p99 | > 800ms for 5m |\n| `api_latency_p99_write_burn` | write-path p99 (POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE) | > 1500ms for 5m |\n| `kernel_consumer_lag` | `kernel.consumer.lag` | > 60s for 5m |\n| `kernel_notification_failure_rate` | notify failure rate | > 1% for 5m (SLO success > 99%) |\n\nThis table is a read-only mirror for context \u2014 the alert policies themselves are Terraform-managed in `infra/envs/stg/monitoring.tf` / `infra/envs/stg/variables.tf`, not edited from Grafana."
      }
    }
  ],
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "window_seconds",
        "type": "query",
        "hide": 2,
        "refresh": 2,
        "datasource": {
          "type": "grafana-postgresql-datasource",
          "uid": "postgres-analytics"
        },
        "query": "SELECT GREATEST(1, (${__to}::bigint - ${__from}::bigint) / 1000)::text AS __value",
        "definition": "Selected time-window duration in seconds",
        "multi": false,
        "includeAll": false,
        "current": {},
        "options": []
      }
    ]
  }
